        "text": "According to Nebraska Solicitor General (Respondents), according to Nebraska Solicitor General (Respondents), respondents (the states) contended that they lacked standing because their alleged injuries\u2014such as reduced tax revenues and alleged harms to MOHELA\u2014were indirect and self\u2011inflicted, and that the HEROES Act does not authorize the Secretary to forgive loan principal."
